<title>CANADA: Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 2.861 pct.</title>
<headline>Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 2.861 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Canada said the average yield at this week's auction of C$2.3 billion of 91-day Government of Canada treasury bills due September 25 was 2.861 percent, up from 2.856 percent last week.</p>
<p>The average yield on C$1.1 billion of 175-day T-bills due December 18 was 3.182 percent, down from 3.194 percent last week, and on C$1.1 billion of 364-day T-bills due June 25, 1998, was 3.670 percent, up from 3.603 percent.</p>
<p>The Bank bought C$600 million three-month, C$100 million six-month and C$100 million one-year bills. It holds C$775 million of C$5.3 billion bills due July 3.  </p>
